        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T21:12:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The first checks whether we\u0027re allowed to Vconn source (not connected to a CTVPD, 5V rail on) and the other checks whether we\u0027re already sourcing.  tc_is_vconn_src() used to integrate the condition of being unable to source as a \u003c 0 return but doesn\u0027t anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "8d0bb029_119cbf0f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4936,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 4936,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "3816196f4dc48e317ee4a0abe87b9535be544274",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8e77d80_5361934b",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4936,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T23:01:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is mean is, if we are already sourcing (tc_is_vconn_src \u003d\u003e 1), and thus don\u0027t want to swap away, does it matter whether we would be able to?\n\nIf tc_check_vconn_swap were removed here, the case where we couldn\u0027t swap if we wanted to but wouldn\u0027t want to anyway, because we are sourcing, would now produce a Reject instead of a Wait. In this scenario, will there ever be a point in the future when we might Accept the VCONN Swap Request? Will we ever give up VCONN?",
      "parentUuid": "fb06a73b_ba5360b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4936,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 4936,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "3816196f4dc48e317ee4a0abe87b9535be544274",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e2e72758_006d9065",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4936,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-29T15:06:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re sourcing but the board code believes we\u0027re unable to source, we should probably accept the vconn swap rather than sending a wait.  It\u0027s a little tricky because tc_check_vconn_swap is both checking that the board is ready to source Vconn (has some 5V rail up, usually), and is allowed to swap (checking CTVPD flag).  These might need to be separated out in order to be handled correctly (though also pending WG discussion).",
      "parentUuid": "b8e77d80_5361934b",
